    <section class="w-full px-4 lg:px-0 bg-white flex justify-center">
        <div class="container w-full max-w-c flex-col lg:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-12 py-12">
                <div class="container w-full max-w-c flex-col lg:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-12 py-12">
                    <h1 class="border-b font-cinzel w-full text-4xl">Baptism</h1>
                </div>
                <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row md:gap-12 md:mb-0 mb-6">

                    <div class="flex-1 mb-12">
                        <p>Baptism is “the basis of the whole of Christian life, the gateway to life in the Spirit, and the door which gives access to the other sacraments.” - Catechism of the Catholic Church, para. 1213.</p>
                        <p>In order to be baptized at St. Emile, a family should be registered and practising members of St. Emile Parish.  If a family is registered in another parish and wishes their infant or child(ren) to be baptized at St. Emile, a letter of permission from the other parish’s pastor is necessary.</p>
                        <p>St. Emile Parish has three baptism preparation methods:</p>
                        <ol class="mb-4 list-decimal list-inside">
                            <li>Infant</li>
                            <ul class="ml-8 list-outside">
                                <li>For newborns to children under the age of five.</li>
                                <li>Please complete the <a href="{{ asset('/documents/2026/2/Baptism Registration Form - INFANT.pdf')}}" target="_blank">Infant Baptism registration form</a>, attach a scan of the infant’s birth certificate, and send these to the office at <a href="mailto:st-epastor@shaw.ca">st-epastor@shaw.ca</a>.</li>
                                <li>Infant baptism asks parents to make the decision to baptize the child and are supported in this decision by godparents.</li>
                            </ul>
                            <li>Child</li>
                            <ul class="ml-8 list-outside">
                                <li>For children between the ages of 5 and 17. </li>
                                <li>Please complete the <a href="{{ asset('/documents/2026/2/Baptism Registration Form - CHILD.pdf')}}" target="_blank">Child Baptism registration form</a>, attach a scan of the child’s birth certificate, and send these to the office at <a href="mailto:st-epastor@shaw.ca">st-epastor@shaw.ca</a>.</li>
                                <li>Children must attend catechism classes as a pre-requisite to baptism. School age children are formed in faith, are taught to discern and use age-appropriate reason independent of (though guided by) their parents and godparents.</li>
                            </ul>
                            <li>Adults</li>
                            <ul class="ml-8 list-outside">
                                <li>People age 18 and up are enrolled in the Rite of Christian Initiation for Adults (RCIA).</li>
                                <li>RCIA is a yearlong education program that begins in September and culminates with the sacraments of Baptism, First Communion, and Confirmation at the Easter Vigil. </li>
                                <li>Please contact Deacon Gilles Urquhart directly (at <a href="tel:2042335114">204-233-5114</a>) to register yourself in RCIA or to offer your services as a sponsor.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </ol>
                        <p>Infant and Child registration forms, once received by the Parish office and reviewed for completeness, are reviewed by the pastor, Father Vincent. Father meets with the parents and after discussion refers them as follows:</p>
                        <p>Infant: Parents and godparents attend a refresher seminar about the Sacrament of Baptism. The pastor will provide credentials to register for this one-hour long seminar. At the end of the seminar, parents can schedule the infant’s baptism with the Baptism Seminar Convener. </p>
                        <p>Child: Parents register their child(ren) for regularly-scheduled catechism classes by e-mailing <a href="mailto:stemilecatechism@gmail.com">stemilecatechism@gmail.com</a> and working with St. Emile’s Religious Education Coordinator to register in the appropriate class. At the end of the program, parents can schedule the child(ren)’s baptism with either the Religious Education Coordinator or the Baptism Seminar Convenor. </p>
                        <p>Adults registered in RCIA with Deacon Gilles are not required to meet with the pastor to proceed. </p>
                        <p class="underline">
                            Important note about godparents: 
                        </p>
                        <ul class="ml-8 list-outside">
                            <li>Only one godparent is required. If there are two godparents, one must be a woman and the other a man.  </li>
                            <li>At least one godparent must have received the Sacrament of Confirmation, be at least 16 years old, and be a practising Catholic in good standing. “Good standing” means, for instance, that if the prospective godparent is married, he or she is married in the Church.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p>
                            Please direct any questions about the Sacrament of Baptism to <a href="mailto:st-epastor@shaw.ca">st-epastor@shaw.ca</a>. 
                        </p>
